gods will be watching isn't quite like  any game I've played before you play it  like a point-and-click adventure but  it's not about solving the kinds of  puzzles you usually find in such games  instead gods will be watching is a  science fiction thriller that puts you  in incredibly high-stakes situations  where the tension is so thick as to be  almost uncomfortable lives hang in the  balance and there are about a million  ways things can go wrong at any moment  consider the first chapter a hostage  situation in which you and the other  members of your resistance group are  trying to hack into a computer belonging  to the holistic Empire you've got four  hostages to manage and enemy soldiers  advancing on your position if any  hostage gets too relaxed he or she will  think you're distracted and make a run  for it if they get too nervous they'll  panic and also make a run for it  either way it's bad news for them but  it's bad news for you to run out of  hostages and the enemy soldiers will  blast their way in every time you take  an action the mood of the hostages  shifts and you need to pay close  attention to their animations to  determine how they're feeling you've  also got to keep the guards at bay and  you've also got a computer to hack and  you've got to regularly reinforce your  network security so that the Empire's  hacker can't counter hack you and cost  you valuable hacking progress it's a lot  of plates to keep spinning and the fact  that people start dying if things go  sideways makes this first chapter a real  pressure cooker the second chapter is  more unpleasant it's a prolonged torture  sequence in which you need to survive  session after session of punishment by  alternating between successfully lying  to your captors provoking them begging  them for mercy and maybe confessing the  occasional detail you have to take the  methods your captors are using to  torture you into account to determine  just how much punishment you can take  since some things hurt a lot more than  others despite the low level of detail  in the graphics I squirm uncomfortably  in my seat every time my characters are  tortured and one round of torture is a  game of Russian roulette in which every  pull of  trigger translates into a chance that  your character's head will be blown off  it's emotionally grueling I guess I  can't complain too much  my characters suffer and die and while I  cringe uncomfortably in sympathy I'm  sitting here comfortably at my computer  but still something about this game  leaves my spirit feeling a little broken  I admire the originality of gods will be  watching but when I meet a brutal end  after suffering through session after  session of digital torture I need to  take some time to recover before jumping  back in and trying it again the gods may  be watching but they're not going to  show you any mercy they're just sitting  in quiet judgment of your every decision  the game will be released for PC on July  24th  you
 

